  "question": "Let $S$ be the set of those real numbers $x$ for which the identity $\\sum_{n=2}^{\\infty}\\cos^n x=(1+\\cos x)\\cot^2x$ is valid, and the quantities on both sides are finite. Then",
  "options": {
    "A": "$S$ is the empty set.",
    "B": "$S=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R:x\\ne n\\pi\\text{ for all }n\\in\\mathbb Z\\}$",
    "C": "$S=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R:x\\ne2n\\pi\\text{ for all }n\\in\\mathbb Z\\}$",
    "D": "$S=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R:x\\ne(2n+1)\\pi\\text{ for all }n\\in\\mathbb Z\\}$"
